% A 3-of-3 multisig that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator. Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Miniscript page
%         https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/
%
% The source, as written:
%     thresh(3,pk(key_1),pk(key_2),pk(key_3),older(12960))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     thresh(3,pk(<key 1>),pk(<key 2>),pk(<key 3>),older(12960))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     key 1 <- key_1
%     key 2 <- key_2
%     key 3 <- key_3
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     at least 3 of these 4:
%       a signature by key 1
%       a signature by key 2
%       a signature by key 3
%       the coin at least 12960 blocks old (about 90 days; older(12960))
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base decaying_multisig includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the coin was confirmed in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the spending transaction is in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the coin has been confirmed for *a number* blocks.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.
    the condition *a condition* is met.

the knowledge base decaying_multisig includes:

the Miniscript page is published at "https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/".
the text of the Miniscript page is at "sources/sipa_miniscript.txt".

the policy in Minsc is published at "https://min.sc/#c=//%20A%203-of-3%20multisig%20that%20turns%20into%20a%202-of-3%20after%2090%20days%0A//%20The%20Logical%20English%20twin's%20policy%20(the%20Miniscript%20translator%20of%20Logical%20English).%0A$key_1%20=%2002a1baf00e3034a5edcb96dc4ce597e523845690eec754848d9921778f6de46833;%20%20%20//%20key%201%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$key_2%20=%20030b078407422b0b5578954183d643842de93e7db886add339708f68547bd87f8c;%20%20%20//%20key%202%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$key_3%20=%20038e1d0c4261f914859fd50f3fc02bff1c919db2bee4ec6530df824d3305b8ae5a;%20%20%20//%20key%203%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A%0Athresh(3,pk($key_1),pk($key_2),pk($key_3),older(12960))%0A".

the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is published at "https://tape.rewindbitcoin.com/explorer/address/bcrt1qw6n9myd32gkhhjqeg65z0pxkg3cqhk7ysk3ptum7gpy4ujur07lq84wupe".
the text of the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is at "sources/decaying_multisig.chain.json".

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule decaying_threshold with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A 3-of-3 that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days":
the coin can be spent if
    a number N is the count of each C such that
        a condition C is in [the signature of key 1, the signature of key 2, the signature of key 3, the delay of 12960 blocks]
        and the condition C is met
    and N >= 3.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_1 with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A 3-of-3 that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days":
the condition the signature of key 1 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 1.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_2 with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A 3-of-3 that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days":
the condition the signature of key 2 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 2.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_3 with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A 3-of-3 that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days":
the condition the signature of key 3 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 3.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_4 with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A 3-of-3 that turns into a 2-of-3 after 90 days":
the condition the delay of 12960 blocks is met if
    the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks
    and N >= 12960.

% The age of the coin, which the relative timelocks (older) measure.
rule coin_age_in_blocks:
the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks if
    the coin was confirmed in block a height H
    and the spending transaction is in block a height M
    and N = M - H.

scenario decaying_threshold_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path decaying_threshold_1 — the path needs: a coin 12960 blocks old, a signature by key 1, a signature by key 2
    the witness contains a signature by key 1.
    the witness contains a signature by key 2.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

