scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by key 1", "add: the witness contains a signature by key 2", "add: the witness contains a signature by key 3"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by key 1", "add: the witness contains a signature by key 2"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by key 1", "add: the witness contains a signature by key 3"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by key 2", "add: the witness contains a signature by key 3"]].

scenario lost_key_1 is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of key 1 lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by key 2.
    the witness contains a signature by key 3.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the coin was confirmed in block 850000"], ["remove: the spending transaction is in block 862960"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by key 2"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by key 3"]].

scenario lost_key_2 is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
